From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] nx2: the write-back scratch growth of EDEN_NX2_DEFER_WRITEBACK_OOM is optional: not tried when the pool is too small, refused at once otherwise (waveydude's 0918), off by default

What: 0662 grows the swizzle scratch before an eviction's write-back and keeps the image when the
growth is refused. That growth runs on the GPU thread. Without this patch a refusal first goes
through operator new's handler (headless/main.cpp): the door wait (EDEN_UP_DOOR_WAIT), the
EDEN_UP_NEW_WAIT_MS wait, the EDEN_HEAP_FAILURE line and a heap snapshot, all for an allocation the
collector can do without.

Now, inside ReserveEvictionWritebackScratch only (so only with EDEN_NX2_DEFER_WRITEBACK_OOM=1):
- when the pool's largest free block is known (eden_pool_largest_free, headless/performance.cpp)
  and smaller than the growth, it is not tried: the image stays for a later pass;
- otherwise the growth runs inside eden_optional_allocation_scope (wrapper, headless/main.cpp, part
  of this commit): while a thread's depth is not 0, the new handler throws bad_alloc at once. The
  scope ends with the block (SCOPE_EXIT), also when the growth throws.
Both hooks are weak and PS5_NATIVE only: without them the growth is tried as in 0662.

Off: ReserveEvictionWritebackScratch returns before any of this, the depth stays 0, and the handler's
only new work is one thread-local load, on a refusal. Not in the kept-store stamp.

Risk: the largest free block counts the pool, not the free room inside the heap's own spaces, so
it can say no to a growth the heap could have served from its arenas. The image then stays dirty
until the pool has a block that size (no loss, but less memory freed by that pass).

Origin and credit: waveydude, patch 0918 ("Skip memory waits for optional texture writeback
scratch") and its wrapper half (eden_optional_allocation_scope in headless/main.cpp), commit
c7ee4d0.
---
diff --git a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
index d5210db..e60ce70 100644
--- a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@
 #include <boost/container/small_vector.hpp>
 
 #include "common/alignment.h"
+#include "common/scope_exit.h"
 #include "common/settings.h"
 #include "common/slot_vector.h"
 #include "video_core/control/channel_state.h"
@@ -506,6 +507,14 @@ TextureCache<P>::TextureCache(Runtime& runtime_, Tegra::MaxwellDeviceMemoryManag
     }
 }
 
+#ifdef PS5_NATIVE
+// headless/performance.cpp: the pool's largest free block in bytes, 0 when unknown. headless/main.cpp
+// (0663): while a thread is inside this scope, operator new's handler refuses at once (no wait, no
+// failure line). Weak: without them the growth below is tried as it is.
+extern "C" unsigned long long eden_pool_largest_free(void) __attribute__((weak));
+extern "C" void eden_optional_allocation_scope(bool enter) noexcept __attribute__((weak));
+#endif
+
 // EDEN_NX2_DEFER_WRITEBACK_OOM=1 (exact "1"; waveydude's 0913): a block-linear write-back needs
 // scratch for one guest level at a time (SwizzleImage). When it would grow the scratch by a large
 // request (WritebackNeedsHeap: not a host span, not covered by the write-back bands, 256 KiB or
@@ -526,7 +535,28 @@ TextureCache<P>::TextureCache(Runtime& runtime_, Tegra::MaxwellDeviceMemoryManag
     if (required <= scratch.capacity()) {
         return true;
     }
+#ifdef PS5_NATIVE
+    // waveydude's 0918: the image can stay for a later pass, so this growth is optional. When the
+    // pool's largest free block is known and smaller, it is not tried at all; when it is tried, a
+    // refusal comes back at once instead of waiting in operator new's handler on the GPU thread.
+    if (eden_pool_largest_free) {
+        const unsigned long long largest = eden_pool_largest_free();
+        if (largest != 0 && largest < required) {
+            return false;
+        }
+    }
+#endif
     try {
+#ifdef PS5_NATIVE
+        if (eden_optional_allocation_scope) {
+            eden_optional_allocation_scope(true);
+        }
+        SCOPE_EXIT {
+            if (eden_optional_allocation_scope) {
+                eden_optional_allocation_scope(false);
+            }
+        };
+#endif
         scratch.resize_destructive(required);
         return true;
     } catch (const std::bad_alloc&) {
